==Strategy==
It's possible to stall Teacher Bun Bun using constant meatshields until you're able to summon [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], but clearing the first few Heavenly Hippoes is the main problem. For Li'l Nyandam, it is recommended to bring [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red cats]] such as [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]], [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]], [[Swordsman Cat (Rare Cat)|Sword Master Cat]], etc. For the Le'noirs, [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl/Pizza Cat]] will be your best friend for dealing with them.

Money is only an issue at the start, since the occasional Shy Boys and Wall Doges that spawn will give you a good amount of cash once killed later on, so your main goal is to kill each "mini-boss" that comes to support Li'l Nyandam before tackling him. Le'noirs will mostly act as a wall to protect Nyandam and won't pose much of a threat unless your main attacks against them are very slow or have low health. Metal Doges will be a huge nuisance, but with enough meatshields, or any unit able to do a [[Critical Hit]], like [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat Sitter]], they'll be taken care of. (Since they only take 1 damage from any attack, your meatshields can shred their health since they will, most of the time, be able to get 1 or 2 hits in before larger enemies kill them). The Heavenly Hippoes and Bun Bun at the start could be hard to deal with, but as said before, Bahamut Cat can take care of them consistently, alternatively [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] and/or [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] can also deal with them. Li'l Nyandam himself isn't too hard to deal with on his own, given he's basically the same as [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]], except for a little bit of extra range and a faster attack rate, so once the other threats are taken care of, you've basically won the stage.

Additionally, with the presence of the power-house that is [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], if one is lucky enough to already have him, he makes this stage much easier, as he can deal very good damage to basically every enemy here, and can eat huge chunks of health from the Shy Boys and Li'l Nyandam once he can reach him. [[Fedora Cat (Special Cat)|Fedora Cat]], while having less DPS than Courier and being a limited unit, can act as a replacement with his higher standing range, which could help in stacking them, though he won't be as useful in general as he is pretty fragile and his cooldown is pretty long, even with his [[Blue Strike (Combo)|Combo]].

